{"id":"H6411","lemma":"פְּלָאיָה","transliteration":"pelayah","sayIt":"pe-la-YAH","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"","gloss":"Pelaiah","meaning":"A man living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at Neh.8.7\n§ Pelaiah = \"Jehovah does wonders\"\n1) son of Elioenai and a descendant of David in the royal line\n2) a priest who helped Ezra to expound the law to the people and also sealed the covenant with Nehemiah","glosses":["pelaiah","instructed the people in"],"count":3,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"1ch-3","v":24,"renderings":{"bsb":"Pelaiah","kjv":"and Pelaiah"}},{"chapterId":"neh-8","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"instructed the people in","kjv":"Pelaiah"}},{"chapterId":"neh-10","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"Pelaiah","kjv":"Pelaiah"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"1 Chronicles 3:24","note":"The sons of Elioenai: Hodaviah, Eliashib, Pelaiah, Akkub, Johanan, Delaiah, and Anani, seven.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Nehemiah 8:7","note":"Also Jeshua, Bani, Sherebiah, Jamin, Akkub, Shabbethai, Hodiah, Maaseiah, Kelita, Azariah, Jozabad, Hanan, Pelaiah, and the Levites, caused the people to…","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H0454","lemma":"אֶלְיְהוֹעֵינַי","transliteration":"elyehoenay","gloss":"Eliehoenai"},{"id":"H0475","lemma":"אֶלְיָשִׁיב","transliteration":"elyashiv","gloss":"Eliashib"},{"id":"H1806","lemma":"דְּלָיָ֫הוּ","transliteration":"delayah","gloss":"Delaiah"},{"id":"H1938","lemma":"הוֹדַוְיָה","transliteration":"hodavyah","gloss":"Hodaviah"},{"id":"H3110","lemma":"יוֹחָנָן","transliteration":"yochanan","gloss":"Johanan"},{"id":"H6054","lemma":"עֲנָנִי","transliteration":"anani","gloss":"Anani"},{"id":"H6126","lemma":"עַקּוּב","transliteration":"aqquv","gloss":"Akkub"},{"id":"H1939","lemma":"הוֹדַיְוָהוּ","transliteration":"hodayvahu","gloss":"Hodaiah"}],"senses":[{"id":"H6411B","gloss":"Pelaiah","relation":"H6411B ="}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}